    ! ---- pf_random_normal_at / pf_random_normal_portable_at ----
    !
    ! The scalar grid, plus coordinates hunted deterministically until every branch
    ! is represented: a table built from the grid alone would be ~98.5 %% path 1 and
    ! would leave the wedge and tail unpinned, so a change to either would move no
    ! golden value at all.
    !
    ! norm_zig_path  1 immediate rectangle acceptance, 2 wedge test, 3 tail.
    ! norm_zig_pairs / norm_polar_pairs  word PAIRS the rejection loop consumed. The
    !                consumption is contract for the stream walk, and a table with no
    !                entry above the minimum would pass against a loop that never
    !                rejects anything.
    !
    ! **The two columns are pinned to different strengths, and the reason is the
    ! algorithms rather than a choice.** The polar form is exact bit contract on
    ! every platform: IEEE + - * / and sqrt over the frozen logarithm, nothing else.
    ! The Ziggurat reaches libm `exp` in its wedge test and libm `log` in its tail,
    ! so a path-2 or path-3 row is only bit-identical FOR A GIVEN libm -- which is
    ! exactly what pf_normal_algorithm promises for it. A path-1 row touches no libm
    ! and is exact everywhere. The suite asserts accordingly.
